Frame 0's six failures are ALL preset 6; preset 8 key frames are 12/12. This is
a still divergence reached through the video configuration, and it is a
different surface from real_image_matrix.sh's 180/180 (CID22-512, all-intra,
512x512, presets {2,6,10}).

CONTROL, same cell shape (128x128 q40 p6 frames=2): synthetic `gradient` is
byte-identical on BOTH frames, with frame 1 at 24 bytes -- a skip. The synthetic
inter surface was green because it was asserting a skip frame.

VACUITY NOTE. The first extraction pass scored vidyo3 at mean motion 20.4 and
produced a cell where |f1-f0| was exactly 0.00: all six clips are 30 fps
material published at 60, so every frame is doubled. C and the port both coded
that frame to an identical 24 bytes. mk_video_assets.py now decimates
duplicates and scores motion as the MINIMUM over consecutive pairs, so a
repeated frame cannot be mistaken for parity.
